OpenWings patch 0026: the assistant knows who it is, answers once, and imports Hermes

An owner on a Grok model got "I'm Grok, an AI built by xAI", "I don't have
the ability or tools", a bare "No." and three answers glued into one
message. The model never got an OpenWings identity (Chat mode sent only the
prompt safety policy, Agent mode "You are an AI assistant"), the page sent
Chat mode (no tools) by default while showing Agent, one tool error switched
everyone to Chat mode for good, and the agent supervisor's rejected rounds
were still released by the completion gate. The text and the import live in
OpenWings' own modules (wings/assistant_identity.py, wings/hermes_import.py,
wings/hermes_routes.py, wings/brand/hermes-pack.sh); this patch wires them in:

  * src/chat_processor.py, routes/chat_helpers.py: one trusted identity
    message comes first in every Chat and Agent turn: "You are OpenWings",
    the model and provider, what this install can do for the person, what
    is outside its reach and the way that works instead, and never answering
    with only "No". Stable per person, mode and model (prompt cache safe).
  * src/agent_loop.py: the competing "You are an AI assistant" lines go;
    the full tool inventory route keeps the identity; refusal rules ask for
    the reason and the way that works; grok models get native tools on any
    OpenAI compatible host; the local machine rules say the container cannot
    read the person's computer; a true refusal about something outside
    OpenWings (another app, files on the host) is not nudged again; the
    intent and clarification nudges retract the round they reject.
  * src/agent_runtime/completion.py: the gate releases only the rounds the
    loop kept, with a blank line between kept rounds, so rejected drafts are
    neither shown nor saved (they were glued: "memory.No, I still cannot").
  * static/app.js, static/js/chat.js, static/js/compare/index.js: Agent is
    the default mode (as the page already showed); a tool error no longer
    saves Chat mode for every later chat, it says what happened and what to
    do; a turn_mode event lets wings-hermes.js note once that Chat mode has
    no tools.
  * static/js/wings-hermes.js, static/index.html: Import from Hermes in the
    Memory window (Memories and Add tabs, Settings tab with past imports and
    Undo) and from any #import-hermes link: the one line Terminal command,
    upload or pasted text, preview with counts and ticks, import, Undo.
    Imported chats open read only with "Start a new chat".
  * src/tool_capabilities.py: the chat preface's "available skills index"
    is server owned metadata like "skills", so it no longer marks every
    agent turn as externally tainted ("external untrusted context blocks
    read_private" when asked about memory).
  * src/turn_contract.py: a question about another assistant's memory or
    chats (Hermes) is not sealed into a read of OpenWings' own memory, which
    answered "No saved memories found." instead of the import path.
  * app.py, routes/chat_routes.py, routes/history/history_routes.py,
    routes/session_routes.py: the Hermes routes, and a 409 with one plain
    sentence for any change to a chat imported from Hermes.
  * tests/test_openwings_assistant_identity.py,
    tests/test_supervisor_retracted_rounds.py: the identity in both modes,
    the owner's glued answer as a regression test, the gate separator;
  * tests/test_foreground_model_routing.py: a promise only round the
    intent nudge rejects is retracted, so provenance follows the answer.

